  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0093 database is a collection of tables that store information about various aspects of basketball. The tables include:\n* awards_players: This table contains information about awards won by players, including the player's ID, the award, the year it was won, the league they played in, and any notes.\n* coaches: This table contains information about coaches, including their ID, their full name, the year they coached, the team they coached, the league they coached in, the number of times they coached, the number of wins and losses they had, and any additional information.\n* draft: This table contains information about players who were drafted, including the year they were drafted, the round they were drafted in, the selection they were drafted at, the overall pick they were drafted as, the team they were drafted by, and any additional information.\n* players: This table contains information about players, including their ID, their first and last name, their position, the year they first played, the year they last played, their height and weight, their college, any additional information, and their death date.\n* players_teams: This table contains information about the teams a player played for, including the player's ID, their name, the year they played, the stint they played, the team they played for, the league they played in, and any additional information.\n* series_post: This table contains information about the playoff series, including the year, the round, the series, the winning team, the losing team, and any additional information.\n* teams: This table contains information about teams, including their ID, their league, their franchise ID, their conference ID, their division ID, their rank, their playoff status, their seed, their first round, their semifinals, their finals, their name, and any additional information.\n* teams_post: This table contains information about the playoff teams, including the year, the team's ID, their league, their wins, and losses, and any additional information.\nEach table has its own set of columns, with some tables having foreign keys that reference other tables. For example, the awards_players table has a foreign key that references the players table, and the players_teams table has foreign keys that reference both the players table and the teams table. The tables also have primary keys, unique constraints, and composite keys to ensure data integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context  \nThe project involves developing a predictive analytics system for a women's basketball database. The key task is to predict whether a team will qualify for the playoffs based on historical and seasonal data.\n\nObjectives  \n- To accurately predict playoff participation for basketball teams.\n- To utilize player, team, and game statistics for predictive modeling.\n- To enhance decision-making for coaches and analysts through data insights.\n\nStakeholders & Users  \n- Basketball Coaches  \n- Team Analysts  \n- Sports Statisticians  \n- Basketball League Officials\n\nFunctional Descriptions  \n1. Data Input and Storage:  \n   - Collect and store player statistics, team performance data, awards, and draft details.\n   - Integrate historical game performance data from the database.\n\n2. Predictive Analytics:  \n   - Analyze team and player statistics to predict playoff outcomes.\n   - Utilize machine learning models for prediction based on current and historical data.\n\n3. Reporting and Visualization:  \n   - Generate reports on team likelihood of playoff participation.\n   - Provide visual analytics dashboards for user-friendly insights.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions  \n- Performance: Must handle and process data for multiple seasons without performance degradation.\n- Scalability: Support increased data load as more seasons and teams are added.\n- Security: Ensure sensitive data such as player information is securely handled and stored.\n- Usability: Interface should be intuitive for non-technical users such as coaches and sports analysts.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0093.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0093\nCREATE TABLE `awards_players` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `player_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `award` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `league` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `awards_players_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`player_id`) REFERENCES `players` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `coaches` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `full_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `league` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `coaching_times` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `wins` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losses` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `additional_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `draft` (\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `round` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `selection` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `overall_pick` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `additional_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`year`, `round`, `selection`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `players` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `year_first_played` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `year_last_played` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `height` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `weight` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `college` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `additional_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `death_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `players_teams` (\n  `player_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `player_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stint` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `league` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `additional_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`player_id`, `year`, `stint`),\n  CONSTRAINT `players_teams_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`player_id`) REFERENCES `players` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `players_teams_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `series_post` (\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `round` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `series` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_team` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_team` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `additional_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`year`, `round`, `series`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `league` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `franchise_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `conference_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `division_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rank` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `playoff_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `seed` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_round` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `semifinals` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `finals` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `additional_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams_post` (\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `league` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `wins` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losses` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `additional_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`year`, `team_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teams_post_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
